      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's exhausting to keep pretending, especially when the core of who you were has dissolved. That feeling of being a hollow shell is a very real, very heavy thing to live with. Instead of trying to force yourself to feel \"better,\" maybe just focus on the immediate, quiet relief of letting go of the performance. A single, small act of self-kindness, like a deep breath or a moment of stillness, can be a tiny step away from the crushing weight of expectation.",
